{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}SVN keywords setup in  PHP IDE ( Zend  Studio){% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Best Practice</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">SVN keywords setup in  PHP IDE ( Zend  Studio)</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            
            {% include '@partial/left-menu.html.twig' %}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">SVN keywords setup in  PHP IDE ( Zend  Studio)</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> Best Practice
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        For a better integration of SVN, your PHP IDE( Zend Studio), and a bug tracker of choice, the below proprieties must be set, <strong>for each project</strong> you have.

<!--more-->

Right click on <strong>project</strong>
Go to <strong>Team-&gt;Set Propriety</strong>
<ul>
	<li>SVN Ignore files, below you have an example. As we do not want to commit your local settings
to the main repository :-)</li>
</ul>
<pre class="bash"><strong>Name:</strong> svn:ignore
<strong>Propriety:</strong>
*.project
*.prefs
.project
cache
.settings
.buildpath
*.ini</pre>
<ul>
	<li>Basic integration with a bug tracker</li>
</ul>
<pre class="bash"><strong>Name:</strong> bugtracq:label
<strong>Propriety:</strong> Tracker ID:</pre>
<pre class="bash"><strong>Name:</strong> bugtraq:message
<strong>Propriety:</strong> </pre>
<ul>
	<li>If you have a public bug tracker system , example Mantis</li>
</ul>
<pre class="bash"><strong>Name:</strong> bugtraq:url
<strong>Propriety:</strong> http://www.dotkernel.net/view.php?id=%BUGID%</pre>
For <strong>above</strong> Proprieties , apply <strong>only</strong> to project folder, <strong>NOT</strong> recursive
<h3>Final step( below instructions are good <strong>only</strong> for <strong>svn:keywords</strong> )</h3>
&nbsp;

Check the <strong>Apply property recursively to:</strong>
Select <strong>All resources</strong>
Check the <strong>Use filtration by the resource name </strong> and add <strong>Mask: </strong>*.php

<a href="http://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/svn-add.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1980" alt="svn-add" src="http://www.dotkernel.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/svn-add.jpg" width="589" height="668" / class="img-fluid rounded my-2"></a>
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>
            
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}